FULL CURSOR PROMPT — PayPal as a Payment Option for One-Time Payments
Important — check existing code first: Before building anything, inspect the existing Stripe Connect integration, specifically how payments are currently processed for tipping (Tip Room, Live Request Room, in-player tipping), event ticket purchases, and any audio material/merchandise purchases. Check whether Stripe Checkout is already configured to support PayPal as a payment method within the existing Stripe integration (Stripe supports this natively in many regions), since this may significantly reduce the scope of this work versus building a separate, standalone PayPal SDK integration.
What to build:
Add PayPal as an available payment method for all existing one-time payment flows: Tip Room tips, Live Request Room tips, in-player music tipping, live audio session tips, event ticket purchases, and audio material/merchandise purchases. Subscriptions are explicitly out of scope for this prompt.
Approach, in priority order:
First, check if enabling PayPal within the existing Stripe Checkout configuration is sufficient to cover this requirement. If so, this is a configuration change plus checkout UI update, not a new integration, implement it this way.
Only if Stripe's native PayPal support is unavailable or insufficient for the required flows, build a separate PayPal integration (using PayPal's official SDK) as a genuinely separate payment option alongside Stripe at checkout.
UI requirement:
Wherever a payment method selection currently appears (or where Stripe Checkout is currently embedded) across all the flows listed above, ensure PayPal appears as a selectable option alongside existing card payment methods, using PayPal's standard branded button/UI component, not a custom-built equivalent.
Scope boundaries:
This prompt covers incoming, one-time payments only (tips, ticket purchases, material purchases)
Do NOT include subscription billing anywhere in this prompt
Do NOT change creator payout methods or payout architecture as part of this prompt, this only affects how a payer chooses to pay, not how creators receive funds
General rules:
Follow existing checkout flow styling and component structure throughout
Ensure transaction records store which payment method was used (Stripe card vs PayPal), matching existing transaction schema conventions, for accurate reconciliation and reporting